 and add those numerators so  let's go ahead and distribute the 3x  that's going to give us 3x squared plus  3x over here 4 times 2x is 8x and we're  adding so that's plus 8x let's go ahead  and combine like terms this is going to  give us 11x plus 3x squared all over our  common denominator 10 x squared 10 x  squared times X plus 1 okay now remember  when I was talking about the numerator  you want to see if you can factor it  let's go ahead and do that we can see we  have an X in common here for both of  these so we can factor out an X that's  going to give us 3x plus 11 all over our  common denominator 10 x squared times X  plus 1 you can see here that one of  these X's cancels with one of these X's  leaving one left over and so our final  result here is going to be 3x plus 11  all over 10 x times X plus 1 and  normally I just leave that denominator  factored that's normally how you know  how it's done you don't have to go ahead  and keep multiplying the main thing was  you get the common tab here combine them  together the next step after learning  how to add and subtract rational  expressions is to solve rational  equations again involving getting  common denominators or clearing the  denominator and I talked about that in  that video right there so follow me over  that video and we'll continue on with  this lesson

